--- sys's operations over functions (`describe`, `apply`) are the standard
--- library's own (spec, sys): a program's call of one is refused before it
--- runs — it had passed every check, then the interpreter stopped, "does
--- not run 'describe' yet", and the compiled program did not build
--- (Rosetta Code, Metaprogramming)

fn double[x]
    return x * 2

d = describe[double]
log[d]
